; tempo-map: the piecewise transport under the corpus gate. 120 bpm
; doubling to 240 at beat 4 (tick 720720 — wall-clock 2.0 s), so the
; loop :dur 8b is 3.0 s of wall-clock, not 4.0. Pins, per eval time:
;   - the s-unit key resolves through the map (2.5 s = beat 6, tick
;     1081080 — the constant math would say beat 5);
;   - :emit [beat bpm]: bpm is a STEP function landing exactly at the
;     boundary, bit-identical to what a `(track :expr bpm)` would emit;
;   - loop wraps in SECONDS: 3.5 s replays 0.5 s of SEGMENT 0 (beat 1)
;     — tick-wrapping would land on beat 2 at the wrong tempo.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 8b :end loop :emit [beat bpm])
(tempo :at 4b :bpm 240)

(track :target radius
  (key :at 0b :value 0.0)
  (key :at 2.5s :value 1.0))
